 title='Nivolumab, ipilimumab, pemetrexed and '+plat
 schedule='The first cycle lasts 42 days: all four medicines on Day 1, then nivolumab, pemetrexed and '+plat+' on Day 22. Chemotherapy ends after those two visits. From Cycle 2, nivolumab continues on Days 1 and 22 and ipilimumab on Day 1 of each 42-day cycle.'
 duration='Immune treatment continues while appropriate until the cancer progresses, side effects require stopping, or up to 24 months without progression. Plans can change after review.'
 purpose='This treatment aims to control metastatic non-small-cell lung cancer, help symptoms and extend life. It is usually given without an expectation of cure. The team checks the cancer subtype, molecular results, your health and your preferences before recommending this particular chemotherapy backbone.'
 immune='Nivolumab and ipilimumab can inflame healthy organs. Report new symptoms promptly, including after treatment stops; follow-up vigilance is required for at least five months after the last dose.'
 vitamins='Folic acid starts before pemetrexed, continues through both chemotherapy visits and for 21 days after the last pemetrexed dose. B12 is given in the preceding week. The source repeats B12 every three cycles if pemetrexed continues; this planned course has only two pemetrexed administrations, so do not automatically continue B12 in immune-only cycles.'
 steroids='Your team reconciles the steroid used to prevent pemetrexed rash with the anti-sickness steroid into one clear prescription. Do not add the two schedules together or use leftover steroids yourself.'
 baseline=['Confirm first-line metastatic/recurrent NSCLC, no sensitising EGFR mutation or ALK translocation, ECOG 0–1 and pemetrexed suitability for the histology. Current NCCP wording removed non-squamous; this is not permission to use pemetrexed for every histology.','FBC, renal/liver profile, glucose, thyroid function, hepatitis B surface antigen, hepatitis C RNA and morning cortisol. '+('Measured isotope GFR is preferred for carboplatin; review method, recency and Calvert dose.' if carbo else 'Assess renal function, fluid status and the cisplatin hydration/electrolyte plan.'),'Review significant autoimmune disease, systemic immunosuppression, infection, CNS disease, prior PD-1/PD-L1 treatment, ILD, hearing/tinnitus and neuropathy. Audiology/CrCl if indicated. Confirm folate lead-in and B12.']
 ongoing=['Before EACH treatment on Day 1 and Day 22: FBC and renal/liver profile, symptom/immune-toxicity assessment.','Before EACH 42-day cycle: glucose and TFTs; repeat/add other tests when symptoms or the clinical plan require.','Before the Day 22 induction visit: review counts, kidney function, hearing/nerves and toxicity after the first chemotherapy administration; confirm the second and final planned pemetrexed/platinum doses.']
 administration='Nivolumab over 30 minutes first; ipilimumab over 30 minutes on Day 1 only; pemetrexed over 10 minutes; '+('carboplatin over 30 minutes.' if carbo else 'cisplatin over 60 minutes, starting 30 minutes after pemetrexed, with pre/post hydration.')+' Ipilimumab requires vital signs every 30 minutes during infusion and for one hour afterwards. Clinic time also includes assessment, preparation, observation and support.'
 limitations=['NCCP cycles are 42 days. The trial description of two chemotherapy cycles refers to two 21-day chemotherapy administrations, not two 42-day cycles.','Checkpoint doses are held or stopped, not reduced. If either nivolumab or ipilimumab is withheld, the other is also withheld; any later nivolumab-only plan is a consultant decision.','Current NCCP Table 1 uses CTCAE v4: grade 3 colitis stops both immune drugs, whereas grade 3 creatinine elevation holds them. Do not import another checkpoint regimen’s thresholds.','Chemotherapy-specific modifications cease when chemotherapy ends; ongoing low counts or organ dysfunction still require clinical assessment.','At immune-only Day 1, ipilimumab makes the visit low emetic risk; Day 22 is nivolumab alone and minimal risk. Do not carry the high-risk induction support forward automatically.',steroids]
 clinical={'rationale':{'summary':'Nivolumab blocks PD-1 and ipilimumab blocks CTLA-4, supporting T-cell antitumour activity through different checkpoint pathways. Pemetrexed inhibits nucleotide synthesis and '+plat+' damages DNA. The trial combines limited initial chemotherapy with continuing dual immunotherapy; this rationale does not predict individual response.','setting':'First-line metastatic NSCLC; histology-appropriate pemetrexed backbone','line':'First-line','factors':baseline,'alternatives':['The consultant compares biomarker-directed therapy when appropriate, other immune/chemotherapy options, trials and symptom-focused care in the context of molecular results, fitness and preferences. Supportive/palliative care can accompany anticancer treatment.'],'limitations':limitations,'sources':[{'label':'NCCP '+c+' v4','url':URL[c]},{'label':'CheckMate 9LA final six-year outcomes','url':TRIAL},{'label':'EMA nivolumab','url':EMA['nivo']},{'label':'EMA ipilimumab','url':EMA['ipi']},{'label':'EMA pemetrexed','url':EMA['pem']}]},'key_points':[schedule,duration,administration]+limitations,'patient_selection':{'treatment_intent':purpose,'disease_and_biomarker_context':[p['metadata']['indication']],'eligibility_orientation':baseline,'important_cautions':limitations},'support_summary':[vitamins,steroids,'Induction uses '+('the dedicated high-risk carboplatin AUC ≥4 NCIS row, without routine olanzapine.' if carbo else 'the generic high-risk NCIS row including olanzapine, plus cisplatin hydration and electrolyte care.'),'Immune continuation: low-risk support on Day 1, minimal-risk on Day 22; retain alert-card and immune symptom education.'],'baseline':baseline,'before_each_cycle':ongoing,'ongoing':[vitamins,immune,'Disease imaging and additional tests follow the consultant plan; no fixed scan interval is asserted.'], 'administration':[administration],'access':['IV treatment through agreed venous access; no home chemotherapy pump.','Arrange transport, lab appointments and prescriptions. '+('Renal testing is needed for the consultant-selected carboplatin AUC 5 or 6.' if carbo else 'Allow extra time for pre/post hydration and review fluid restrictions, urine and electrolyte needs individually.')+' Keep immune alert information available for every healthcare contact.']}
 evidence={'trial':'CheckMate 9LA — final six-year analysis (2025)','population':'719 previously untreated adults with stage IV/recurrent NSCLC without sensitising EGFR/ALK alterations; mixed squamous and non-squamous histologies.','comparison':'Nivolumab plus ipilimumab and two cycles of histology-based platinum-doublet chemotherapy (361) versus four chemotherapy cycles (358); optional pemetrexed maintenance in the control non-squamous population.','applicability':'Supports the overall first-line strategy. The pemetrexed protocols correspond to the non-squamous chemotherapy backbone studied; overall results pool histologies and platinum choices. No separate randomized benefit estimate for this exact '+plat+' backbone is asserted.','endpoints':[{'endpoint':'OS','metric':'Overall randomized population, final six-year analysis','result_text':'HR 0.74 (95% CI 0.63–0.87); six-year survival 16% versus 10%, minimum follow-up 68.6 months.','interpretation':'Population-level randomized comparison of the complete treatment strategies, not a personal survival prediction or a cisplatin-versus-carboplatin comparison.','analysis_status':'Final six-year follow-up; published 29 May 2025.','sources':[{'label':'Carbone et al., ESMO Open 2025','url':TRIAL}]},{'endpoint':'OS','metric':'Non-squamous histology subgroup, six-year survival','result_text':'17% versus 12%.','interpretation':'Descriptive subgroup result; does not isolate pemetrexed/carboplatin from pemetrexed/cisplatin or establish comparative benefit between platinum choices.','analysis_status':'Final follow-up subgroup analysis; retain subgroup limitations.','sources':[{'label':'CheckMate 9LA final six-year report','url':TRIAL}]}],'qualitative_result':'The combined strategy improved survival compared with chemotherapy in the trial population, with some durable responses. Benefits and harms vary between people.','limitations':['The whole-trial result includes squamous and non-squamous disease and different chemotherapy backbones.','Non-squamous subgroup data do not establish a separate survival effect for carboplatin versus cisplatin.','Trial participants and treatment selection differ from an individual patient; the reported survival proportions are not individual benefit predictions.','The current NCCP broad NSCLC wording must not be treated as evidence for a histologically inappropriate pemetrexed backbone.'],'sources':[{'label':'CheckMate 9LA final six-year randomized-trial report','url':TRIAL}],'checked':DATE,'harms':'Combining chemotherapy with dual checkpoint blockade introduces cytotoxic and immune-mediated harms; important inflammation can affect multiple organs and require hospital care or permanent treatment cessation. Final follow-up reported no new safety signals; this does not imply no risk.'}
 stages=['Before starting','Cycle 1 · Day 1','Cycle 1 · Day 22','Cycle 2+ · Day 1','Cycle 2+ · Day 22','Completion / follow-up']
 rows=[{'label':'Blood counts, kidney and liver','cells':['Baseline FBC and renal/liver profile','Review before treatment','Review before second/final chemotherapy','Review before every Day 1 dose','Review before every Day 22 dose','Continue unresolved-toxicity checks per plan']},{'label':'Glucose, thyroid and immune symptoms','cells':['Glucose, TFTs, morning cortisol; HBsAg/HCV RNA','Glucose/TFT before this 42-day cycle; immune symptom review','Immune symptom review; extra tests if indicated','Glucose/TFT before every 42-day cycle; symptom review','Immune symptom review; extra tests if indicated','Symptoms can occur at least five months after last dose']},{'label':'Vitamins and steroids','cells':['Folate lead-in; B12 in preceding week; reconcile steroid plan','Daily folate; rash/antiemetic medicines as prescribed','Final planned pemetrexed: repeat prescribed rash/antiemetic course','No further pemetrexed: complete 21-day folate tail; review other support','No automatic B12/rash steroids or induction antiemetics','Agree stop dates and ongoing medicines; no abrupt steroid taper']},{'label':'Platinum precautions','cells':['Renal method, hearing and nerve review'+('; hydration/electrolytes for cisplatin' if not carbo else '')], 'unused':True}]
